            "type": "reasoning",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "Let me check if centering explains the shift: the first example's shape moved from columns 0-4 to 1-5, which centers it in a 7-wide grid. But the second example doesn't fit that pattern\u2014its shape moved to columns 1-3, not the centered 2-4 or 3-5 I'd expect, so centering alone doesn't explain it.\n\nInstead I'm wondering if the shape gravitates toward the left wall inside the frame border. In the first example the shape's minimum column was 0, and it shifted to 1, matching the interior wall. In the second example it also ended at column 1. Since the shapes fully occupy the interior rows in both cases (no vertical room to move), the gravity must be horizontal, pulling shapes left toward the inner wall\u2014though I'm not yet sure why left is the consistent direction.",
                "type": "reasoning_text"
              }
            ],
